<title>SWEDEN: Swedbank posts 20 pct rise '96 profit.</title>
<headline>Swedbank posts 20 pct rise '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Swedbank reports for the 12 months ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			 5,302  vs   4,423</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (SKR)		 5.50  vs    3.50</p>
<p> Interest net			    10,361  vs  10,326</p>
<p> Loan losses net			  1,546  vs     654</p>
<p> Commission				 3,292  vs   2,599</p>
<p> Total income			    15,850  vs  15,383</p>
<p> Operating costs			  8,897  vs   8,744</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	    6,953  vs   6,639</p>
<p> Capital adequacy ratio (pct)	  13.0  vs   13.9</p>
<p> Earnings per share			13.92 vs   11.91</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll found market expectations for an operating profit of 4.99 billion crowns. -- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
